        "_id" : "68ab96253a0dcb7feb8e151c",
        "_score" : null,
        "_source" : {
          "issueTime" : 1756075557181,
          "openCommentState" : "PUBLIC",
          "createTime" : 1756075557181,
          "readPermission" : "PUBLIC",
          "contentText" : "Here's a bold prediction: Leeds will finish higher than Manchester United this season. Yes, they got absolutely battered by Arsenal, but their performance against Everton was genuinely impressive. Ampadu and Tanaka look like serious talents. They've got what it takes to pick up points against the other teams struggling in the league. As for United, honestly, there's nothing to suggest they'll improve on last year. Dorgu seems limited, Bruno is completely inconsistent, and the rest just aren't cutting it. Sesko might be their only glimmer of hope. They've brought in a couple of players who are, frankly, mid-table specialists, yet their fans expect a top-half finish – shake my head. On reflection, it's probably more about Leeds scraping 12th or 13th, rather than United truly plummeting below that. United will certainly be in a tough spot, so the real question is whether Leeds can seize the opportunity.",
          "likeCount" : 0,
          "id" : "68ab96253a0dcb7feb8e151c",
          "title" : null,
          "userId" : 99677987,
          "matchId" : null,
          "commentCount" : 0
